    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "You are right. I am aware of this problem -- just need to come up with a proper fix that doesn't affect performance (int64 are expensive on GPUs). Right now Triton directly translate to `llvm.mul`, which uses the 2-complements and overflows. Casting inputs to a bigger int type before multiplying is the way to do it but my incur some overhead. I have started working on a fix, which includes specializing kernels so that `get_program_id(dim)` returns int16 on small grids, which would remove the performance overhead in most cases that matter :)",
